# consumer-gifter — delegated registration through the membership allocation
# protocol: a funded gifter node serves an OPEN gifter (no authVerifiers), a
# fundless client node registers through nim_rln_consumer with
# {"delegated":"true",...} and proves. The gifter pays; the client never
# touches the faucet.
#
# Artifacts: rln_gifter_module + libp2p_module are not pinned in this repo's
# flake yet (the gifter needs its register-target fix branch) — run with
#   GIFTER_CHECKOUT=<logos-rln-gifter tree with the fix>
#   LIBP2P_MODULE_CHECKOUT=<logos-libp2p-module tree>
NODES=2
NEEDS_MODULES="lez_core liblogos_lez_rln_module liblogos_rln_module libp2p_module rln_gifter_module nim_rln_consumer"
TARGETS="local"
RUNNER=bash
